xcalculator (0.9.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New Currency Converter mode (Ctrl+Alt+C), with the European Central
    Bank's exchange rates for about 30 currencies. Nothing is downloaded
    until Download Rates is clicked; the rates are kept for offline use.
  * Auto Refresh refreshes the rates every 1 to 30 days (3 to start),
    while Xcalculator is open, or also when it's closed if switched on in
    Preferences (a systemd user timer that only Xcalculator enables).
  * Preferences and Documentation wording reviewed: US English, serial
    commas, and a hint for every setting ending with a period.
  * Documentation pages wrap list items under their own text.

 -- Wesley Hayslip <xl_cheese@hotmail.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

xcalculator (0.9.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Opening Xcalculator again, or File → New Window, opens another window in
    the same program. The windows share the Preferences settings and the
    saved history.
  * Settings and history are now kept in ~/.config/xcalculator/.
  * Every word on screen can be translated (gettext); translators start from
    po/xcalculator.pot.
  * The program is split into modules, one per mode.
  * Built with a small Makefile; the menu entry is now
    io.github.xlcheese.Xcalculator.desktop.

 -- Wesley Hayslip <xl_cheese@hotmail.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

